 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the occupation measure of any ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Infra", "*"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "db823916-09c2-471b-9e6e-fa4a45fd091f"],
 " object."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"4fac03de-6abd-486d-83e2-bcf17104814f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: a mesopoint is a finitely supported measure on the vertex set \
\[LongDash] the ",
 StyleBox["measure",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " layer of the point ontology, sitting above the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraPoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraPoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e3b2de4a-d88c-495c-bf93-3a6f002fc963"],
 " atom and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSet"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraSet", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a28b20d1-f1a6-4de2-8c4d-b6e6cb5479d8"],
 " region."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6b2eb725-2e38-4dce-a7f9-f4f691dafc56"],

Cell["\<\
The name is the point of it. A construction whose answer is a single point in \
the continuum often cannot localise to a single vertex on a graph: the honest \
answer is a blob with weights. That is a point at intermediate resolution, \
and it is a distinct kind of object from a region that merely happens to be \
small.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"04683159-2640-4b4b-8db1-09929e5722e7"],

Cell["\<\
Weights count. They are not probabilities put in by hand \[LongDash] a weight \
of 6 means six geodesics chose that vertex.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"de20eba7-2ca2-480d-889e-f18dac67e691"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Mesopoints are ",
 StyleBox["created at a projection",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ", never propagated. The producers are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"seg", "[", 
   RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aa505a0b-2063-466b-80c4-c8e33cf2a288"],
 " (column occupation), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraMidpoint"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/FindInfraMidpoint", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "7b3b0244-dfaf-4bd7-a8ea-dd631d5463c5"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraGoldenSection"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/\
FindInfraGoldenSection", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "629349ce-f834-4280-bdd2-69c47de3f405"],
 " (layer-band occupation), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["FindInfraShellCenter"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/FindInfraShellCenter",
     "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "15995f2f-3fea-4ac7-9a78-48b17fc34504"],
 " (chord-bisection multiplicity), and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraMeasure"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry/ref/InfraMeasure", 
    "WolframInstitute/SyntheticInfrageometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "85717437-bbfe-4eca-abdd-ece0b81e5b3f"],
 " itself. Weights on an ",
 StyleBox["input", "TI"],
 " do not flow through a construction: a construction reads the support and \
ignores the measure."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2632e759-1dad-456a-8c25-6ea7eb4452f7"],

Cell["Up-coercions, all canonical:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ecaf591f-bf44-43e4-805a-b370713c0107"],

